.TH AMCLI 1 "" "AngouriMath" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amcli \- the AngouriMath terminal, and commands that answer once
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amcli
.br
.B amcli
.I command
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments,
.B amcli
opens the AngouriMath terminal: an F# prompt with AngouriMath loaded.
.PP
With a command,
.B amcli
answers once and exits, without starting F#, so that it can sit in a pipe or a script.
An argument written as
.BR _ ,
or left out, is read from standard input.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI eval " expr"
Evaluates
.I expr
to a number, a boolean, or a + bi. A rational is written as a decimal.
.TP
.BI simp " expr"
Simplifies
.IR expr .
.TP
.BI fsimp " expr"
Simplifies
.I expr
quickly: the normalisation, without the search.
.TP
.BI diff " var expr"
Differentiates
.I expr
with respect to
.IR var .
.TP
.BI solve " var statement"
Solves
.I statement
for
.IR var ,
one root per line when there are finitely many.
.TP
.BI sub " var value expr"
Substitutes
.I value
for
.I var
in
.IR expr .
.TP
.BI latex " expr"
Writes
.I expr
as LaTeX.
.TP
.BI info " expr"
Describes
.IR expr :
its variables, the derivative and the roots for each, and its stationary points, each classified
by the second derivative test.
.TP
.B mcp
Serves the library to an agent over the Model Context Protocol: JSON-RPC on standard input and
standard output, until standard input ends. An MCP client's configuration names
.B amcli
with the argument
.BR mcp .
.B "amcli mcp \-\-selftest"
checks the install, and that the library still behaves as the server's documents say.
.TP
.B help
Lists the commands.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for an answer; 1 when the input does not parse or cannot be answered; 2 for a command that
does not exist or is missing an argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ amcli simp "sin(x)^2 + cos(x)^2"
1
$ amcli solve x "x^2 \- 1 = 0"
1
\-1
$ echo "1 + x^2" | amcli diff x
2 * x
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://am.angouri.org
